c("mandarin-duck", "accepted", "H05", "A Duck on the Railing?", [40180,1840,40500,2160], [40330,2010],
  "One small bird perches on the stone railing above the pond, with a red bill and a sweep of orange and white. The museum's catalogue names mandarin ducks among the painting's birds. Easy to miss; hard to forget once found.",
  "池边石栏上的一只鸳鸯（雄）。故宫著录翎毛列「鴛鴦」。",
  "A small duck with red bill, white eye-stripe, orange-brown cheek and chest, perched on a railing post; about 80 x 160 px.",
  [CAT + " — 主題: 翎毛 鴛鴦"], "V+M", "high", "medium", "One bird only; no 'pair' symbolism.", "Bird confirmed at native size: red bill, white eye-stripe, orange-brown cheek, pale breast, i.e. a drake mandarin duck. Small (about 80 x 160 px): needs the spotlight crop. Promoted by the owner's decision, 2026-11-09.",
  [24,20,14,8,9,4], "Adds a natural detail and a stop in the quiet pond stretch."),
c("antiques", "optional", "H20+H22", "What Is on the Table?", [30420,10,30980,630], [30650,330],
  "Through an open window: a patterned bronze vessel, a white bowl on its stand, a slim vase and stacks of books. The museum counts 'appreciating antiquities' among the scholar's pleasures that Qiu Ying gave to these palace women.",
  "窗内案上陈设：铜器、白瓷碗、瓶、书函。故宫简介提及「鑑古」。",
  "A red-legged table seen through a window, holding a lidded bronze-coloured vessel with a key-fret pattern, a white bowl on a red stand, a small vase and stacked books.",
  [CAT + " — 簡介「琴棋書畫、鑑古、蒔花」; 主題: 器用"], "V+M", "high", "low", "No dynasty or function for any object.", "No one is shown inspecting the objects, so 'appreciating antiquities' is only loosely illustrated. Sits directly above the watering scene.",
  [22,15,13,13,6,4], "Objects are clear, but the story is weaker than the rubric hoped: no group examining them."),
c("hair-flower", "optional", "H07", "A Flower for Your Hair", [27380,1420,27880,2300], [27640,1800],
  "One woman reaches up to tuck a small blossom into her friend's hair. Just behind them, others are picking the branches. It is the quietest kind of spring ritual, and Qiu Ying gave it a corner of its own.",
  "一女子为同伴簪花。属许文美「賞花」段的一部分。",
  "Two standing women face to face; the one on the right raises her hand, holding a small sprig, to the other's hair.",
  [XU + ", Fig. 15 area (賞花)"], "V+S", "high", "medium", "No relationship between the two women.", "Same theme as the accepted flower-picking card; a swap is possible if you prefer this one.",
  [24,18,15,14,5,3], "Charming and clear, but duplicates the flower theme."),
c("stair-child", "optional", "H14", "Up You Come?", [13440,80,14040,870], [13750,400],
  "A small child leans over the stair rail, held by a lady, while a girl below reaches up with both hands. Xu Wenmei places this among the scroll's scenes of playing with infants, a pastime older court paintings loved too.",
  "阶上女子扶幼儿凭栏，阶下少女伸手相逗。许文美图20-2「戲嬰」。",
  "A child with a shaved head leaning over a red stair rail with a woman behind; a figure in green below, back to the viewer, both arms raised toward the child.",
  [XU + ", Fig. 20-2"], "V+S", "high", "high", "No names or relationships.", "Second infant scene; duplicates the accepted one.",
  [25,23,13,13,3,2], "Passes, but only one infant card is needed."),
c("fan-chase", "accepted", "new", "A Fan Raised High", [7050,1680,7520,2420], [7280,2000],
  "A woman in red steps forward with a round fan raised high above her head, sleeves and sash flying. The museum's catalogue lists butterflies in this scroll, and two rest in the willows further left, but none is near her. What caught her eye? The painting leaves it open.",
  "红衣女子举扇疾行，姿态似扑蝶，但其附近并无蝴蝶；两只蝴蝶在左侧约两千像素外的柳树上。故宫著录列「蝶蛾」。",
  "A woman in a red jacket and white skirt in mid-stride, one arm raising a round fan above her head; open ground around her.",
  [CAT + " — 主題: 草蟲 蝶蛾"], "V+M", "high", "low", "Describe only the gesture. Do not say she is catching a butterfly, where she is going or why she hurries.", "Promoted by the owner's decision, 2026-11-09. Fills the long stretch between the portrait and the signature.",
  [22,14,14,14,9,3], "A readable human moment in an otherwise empty stretch; the card asks a question instead of inventing an answer."),

